    "title": "Multiplying a Column-Vector By a Row-Vector"
  },
  "question": {
    ":question/id": "a69f53bb-0b47-5921-abfa-f031f406f62c",
    ":question/problem": "$\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}=$\n\n| {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |\n| {{field-7}} | {{field-8}} | {{field-9}} |\n| {{field-10}} | {{field-11}} | {{field-12}} |",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Here, the first factor is $4\\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n4\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}✓\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 3=4\\times 3\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(-4)\\cdot 5 & (-4)\\cdot (-1) & (-4)\\cdot (-8) \\\\ 0\\cdot 5 & 0\\cdot (-1) & 0\\cdot (-8) \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 5 & (-2)\\cdot (-1) & (-2)\\cdot (-8) \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 5 & (-1)\\cdot (-1) & (-1)\\cdot (-8)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-20 & 4 & 32 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 2 & 16 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
